  "body": "## Overview\n\nAttention sink writes bypassed parameter `weight_loader` callbacks, leaving stale sink values after layerwise reload during RL weight updates. Register checkpoint-backed sinks with a common TP loader and factory, and route model loading through the registered callbacks.\n\nThis consolidates and supersedes #57798, #57801, #57803, #57804, #57805, and #57806.\n\n## Claims\n\n- DeepSeek V4/V4.1, HY-V4, MiMo-V2 (including MTP and Omni MTP), GPT-OSS, Laguna, and Qwen3-DFlash load sinks through their current parameter loader; GPT-OSS preserves MXFP4, Quark and other quantization dispatch.\n- The loader partitions global checkpoint heads once, writes the local shard in place, and restores padded heads to `-inf`. The factory initializes sinks to `-inf` and registers the loader.\n- Regression coverage checks changed sink values across two layerwise reloads, TP sharding, padding, storage preservation, quantization dispatch and pipeline-stage skips.\n\n## Validation\n\n### Current review revision: `7964a96f87`\n\nMerged upstream `main` at `61d9c777bf` before committing the review fixes. Local Windows / Python 3.12 / PyTorch 2.13.0+cpu:\n\n- Isolated CPU regression run: **35 passed, 1 skipped** (CUDA case). Runs the exact repository sink test functions with real PyTorch, unchanged production reload modules, and production model loading methods/helpers extracted from source. It bypasses unrelated vLLM startup imports and model constructors, with stand-ins for unrelated configuration/attention/quantization infrastructure. This is isolated verification, not a standard-suite or full-model run.\n- The six new DeepSeek V4/V4.1 and HY-V4 dispatch cases (TP ranks 0/1) detect an in-memory mutation that loads correct sink values while bypassing the parameter's current loader. Mutation harnesses remain outside the PR.\n- Ruff checks/format, `git diff --check`, SPDX, forbidden-import and test-tethering checks passed.\n- Standard `pytest tests/model_executor/test_weight_utils.py tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_reload.py -k sink -q` remains blocked during startup by missing `uvloop` on Windows. Full pre-commit could not initialize its environments because the configured local proxy is unreachable; commit hooks were bypassed for this revision after the checks above.\n- No remote H20, GPU or full-model validation was performed for this review revision.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Historical H20 validation before this review revision</summary>\n\n### Previous revision\n\nEnvironment: H20 Slurm cluster, node `vllm-h20-02`, 2 x NVIDIA H20-3e, driver 580.105.08; Python 3.12.14 / torch 2.13.0+cu130. Compiled extensions come from the per-commit precompiled cu130 wheel built for this PR's base commit (`vllm-0.31.1rc1.dev295+gd4e92ccc3`) with the branch's Python files overlaid, so Python and extensions are from the same commit without a rebuild.\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pytest tests/model_executor/test_weight_utils.py tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_reload.py -k sink -q` | **41 passed** (GPU node) |\n| full `test_weight_utils.py` + `test_reload.py`, this branch | 18 failed, **110 passed**, 14 skipped, 2 xfailed, 7 errors |\n| full same two files at upstream `main` (control) | 18 failed, 70 passed, 13 skipped, 2 xfailed, 7 errors |\n| failure-name diff, main -> branch | **identical set** (25 names); every additional pass is a sink test |\n| `run-precommit.sh` (every hook the diff touches) | exit 0, no file rewritten |\n| DCO over the branch range | all commits signed off, `DCO pass` |\n\nThe failures are model-download / multi-GPU cases that fail identically before and after the change, so they carry no signal about this PR.\n\nAdditional out-of-tree verification (harness deliberately kept outside the PR, results in the review comments): each sink model's real attention module was built from tiny dimensions with dummy weights on H20, for TP=1 and TP=2, and driven through the real layerwise reload lifecycle, asserting the per-rank slice, the `-inf` padding and the preserved kernel storage; the pre-PR loading shape was reproduced as a control and never received the reloaded sinks.\n\nThese results were recorded before the current review changes and are not a rerun of the current head.\n\n</details>\n\n## Details\n\nA dedicated sink loader derives shard length from the checkpoint rather than the runtime parameter: DeepSeek pads its runtime sink, so `sharded_weight_loader(0)` would use the wrong shard length. Unpadded sinks use the same loader without reconstructing storage. Checkpoint heads must divide evenly across TP ranks.\n\nThe loader keeps the divisibility check and relies on tensor slicing and the default loader for incompatible shapes. Empty checkpoints are no longer explicitly rejected. Lifecycle rationale stays here rather than in long helper docstrings.\n\nTests in the existing CI-selected `test_reload.py` and `test_weight_utils.py` suites cover actual model dispatch for MiMo MTP/Omni MTP, Laguna, DFlash, GPT-OSS, DeepSeek V4/V4.1 and HY-V4. The DeepSeek/HY-V4 tests replace the current loader and verify the unsliced global checkpoint reaches it exactly once for each load. AST factory-name scanning and redundant empty/padding tests were removed.\n\nNo full-model accuracy evaluation, real-checkpoint end-to-end reload, TP>2 or multi-node run was performed. Pipeline parallelism is covered by the skip-path test. Backend-converted sink copies and GPT-OSS expert reload follow-ups are outside this PR; their behavior is unchanged.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Adds focused regression coverage in existing CI-selected suites; validation limits are documented above.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments concise and updates PR documentation.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes scope, validation evidence, root cause, tradeoffs and limitations.\n\n</details>\n",
